\title{Terminology for the parts of an implication}
\date{2026-01-28T20:55:04Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Remark}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{In an [implication](003S) #{P \to Q}, the left-hand proposition #{P} is called the \em{premise} or \em{hypothesis}. #{Q} is called the \em{conclusion}.}

\p{You do not need to memorize these terms, but you should be familiar with them.}
